\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Missing Socks
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 End on the decrypted message. No explanatory diversion.\

\f0\b Verification / aftermath
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 \'93The scientists did all the things the scientists do.\'94\u8232 Establish non-terrestrial origin. Espionage suspects. Gliese 581d ruled out.\

\f0\b The Gibson correlation
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 One remote quake. Timing first. Then the secondary-locus correlation. No local quake. No intentional targeting. No weapons conclusion.\

\f0\b Eloise argues for another test
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 Eloise recognises what encryption + socks implies about the sender. She uses Missing Socks as powerful evidence that the experiment is doing exactly what it was built to do. Gibson is one alarming but unreplicated correlation.\

\f0\b Hosiery Institute diversion
\f1\b0 , probably triggered by Eloise\'92s \'93they\'92re like us\'94 insight.\uc0\u8232 Shorter, much drier, much less pun-driven. Possibly includes the Fred Mason/Gliese 581d parallel.\

\f0\b Return to the argument.
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 Eloise wants replication. Sarah wants understanding before another run. Chip wants the washing machine dismantled and probably buried under something tectonically reliable.\
